<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29393" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŏdŭlātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		modulor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a regular measure</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operis modulationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					5, 9, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dorica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 5,
					9, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incedendi,</span>”
				<i>a marching to time</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 11, 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>a rhythmical measure, modulation;</i>
			hence, <i>singing and playing, melody</i>, in poetry
			and music, <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 139</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modulatione produci aut corripi (verba),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					9, 4, 89</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modulatio pedum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 1,
					6, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scenica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 3, 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vocis,</span>”
				<i>melody</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 3, 59</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">musica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 25, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
